Rime-Jangle
Ingredients: BRITPOP + BREAKBEAT GARAGE & GRIME + MELANCHOLIC, NOSTALGIC & SAD + Theremin
Creative Catalyst: Isolated Svalbard and Hebridean lighthouse keepers broadcast melancholic pirate acoustic sets and syncopated beat tapes across polar sea-lanes during long Arctic nights.

Rime-Jangle is the sound of swaggering, rain-soaked British guitar romanticism colliding with the nocturnal dread and skippy propulsion of London pirate radio. Chime-laden twelve-string acoustic strums, mournful terrace-choir vocals, and aching open chords crash into 134-BPM two-step garage shuffle and heavyweight grime square-bass glides, all haunted by the eerie, microtonal weeping of a Theremin cutting through the salt spray like an automated fog warning.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 132–138 BPM. Skittering, off-grid 2-step garage swing driven by syncopated rimshots, rolling sixteenth-note hi-hat shuffles, and sudden, destabilizing breakbeat downbeats that keep anthemic indie chord progressions perpetually off-balance.
- Harmonic Palette: Natural minor (Aeolian) and Dorian modes, steeped in bittersweet maj7 and add9 open guitar chords, framed against low-register, ominous F-minor and G-minor grime sub-bass glides.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. The Ionospheric Theremin Sweep: Running Theremin portamentos through saturated tape delays and analog pitch-shifters to mimic the mournful, singing wail of marine navigational beacons.
  2. Shortwave RF Saturation: Sidechaining drum buses through crusty vintage AM/shortwave transmitter emulators to create crackling, low-fidelity dynamic compression.
  3. Timber-Room Jangle Tracking: Mic’ing battered acoustic guitars in uninsulated coastal sheds to capture raw fingerboard rattle, immediately juxtaposed against ultra-clean, dry digital sub-bass.
- Dynamics: Songs typically introduce a lonely acoustic fingerpicking pattern or whistling Theremin in near-total silence before exploding into a flurry of crisp, swinging garage breaks; verses remain hushed, claustrophobic, and confessional before swelling into huge, tear-stained Britpop chorus chants underpinned by sub-bass tremors.

Scene & Origin Lore
In the bitter winter of 1997, a handful of isolated relief lighthouse keepers stationed between the outer Hebrides and the Svalbard archipelago began hacking decommissioned VHF naval frequencies to combat the oppressive isolation of six-month polar nights. Armed with waterlogged Tascam four-tracks, battered Rickenbackers, and an Moog Theremin left behind from ionospheric research teams, they spliced bootleg South London 2-step cassettes into pirate broadcasts aimed at passing trawlers and container ships. Coastal dockworkers and rail shunters from Aberdeen to Hull intercepted the transmissions, dubbing them onto bootleg cassettes and birthing a quiet subculture dubbed "Wavelength Lads." Fashion centered around oversized yellow Helly Hansen ocean smocks worn over vintage Umbro tracksuits, salt-stained corduroys, and heavy work boots, with adherents gathering in drafty harbor warehouses and coastal railway sidings to sing terrace-style anthems while skanking over broken garage rhythms.

Typical Instruments: Rickenbacker 360 12-string electric guitar, battered Martin acoustic guitar, Moog Etherwave Theremin, Roland TR-808/909 samples chopped on an Akai S950 sampler, E-mu Orbit sound module (pizzicato strings and square-wave leads), and Shure SM58 microphones wrapped in wool socks.

For Fans Of: The Streets, The Verve, Burial, Doves.

Fictional Band Name: The Gantry Union
Band Description: Formed inside a rusted coastal radar outpost near Peterhead by former North Sea maintenance tech Liam "Ollie" Vance (vocals, 12-string guitar) and pirate radio archivist Maya Lind (Theremin, MPC2000XL breakbeat programming, sub-bass), The Gantry Union are the defining architects of Rime-Jangle. Vance delivers bruised, cigarette-in-the-mist vocal drawls steeped in 1990s northern bravado, while Lind stands enveloped in an oversized fluorescent maritime parka, conjuring spectral, high-register Theremin melodies with precise, gloved hand gestures over ferocious 2-step skanks.
